# Grim Hollow Transformations, chunk c: Ooze, Primordial, Seraph. Own wording.
TRANS = {
 "Ooze": {
  "intro": "You slowly turn into an Ooze, a formless mass of slime. Each stage is a story event, such as being bloodied by an Ooze, suffering experimentation, catching the Weeping Pox, or eating a freshly slain Ooze. Each stage gives new Boons and a new Flaw. Reversing the change takes decades of work and a lot of luck.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain Ooze Form and one other Stage 1 Boon of your choice. You also gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Ooze Form"], "d": "Become an Ooze. Gain Ooze Form, one more Stage 1 Boon, and the Sluggish Flaw."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon. You also gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 2 Ooze Boon and gain the Melted Appearance Flaw."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon. You also gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 3 Ooze Boon and gain the Physical Deterioration Flaw."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon. You also gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 4 Ooze Boon and gain the Slippery Ego Flaw."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Ooze Form": "You are an Ooze in addition to your other creature types. You gain Blindsight with a range of 30 feet. If you already have Blindsight, its range grows by 30 feet. As a Bonus Action, you can manifest your Ooze Form. Your body turns fluid and amorphous, so you can squeeze through a space as narrow as 1 inch without spending extra movement, and you are immune to the Grappled and Restrained conditions. The form lasts 1 minute or until you end it with a Bonus Action. You can manifest it a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage, and you regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Mutable Corpus": "Each time you manifest your Ooze Form, choose one augmentation. **Breathless.** You do not need to breathe. **Disguise.** You reshape your features. You can change your apparent species, look 1 foot taller or shorter, and look heavier or lighter, but your limbs stay arranged the same. A creature can see through it by taking the Study action and succeeding on an Intelligence (Investigation) check against DC 10 plus your Constitution modifier plus your Transformation Stage. **Transparent.** Your body turns see-through, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.",
   "Slimy Mien": "While your Ooze Form is manifested, you are immune to the Charmed condition and your Blindsight range grows by another 30 feet. You can also talk with Oozes within 30 feet as if you shared a language. They are not automatically Friendly toward you, but they do not see you as food and may answer simple questions if they are not Hostile.",
   "Elastic Limbs": "Your limbs stretch and cling. Your reach grows by 5 feet, and you gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. You can climb up, down, and across vertical surfaces and ceilings with your hands free. Creatures you are grappling have Disadvantage on Strength (Athletics) and Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks to escape.",
   "Viscous Durability": "You are immune to the Frightened condition and to Acid damage. When you gain this Boon, choose Cold, Fire, or Lightning. You have Resistance to that damage type.",
   "Corrosive Membrane": "Your Ooze Form lasts 10 minutes when you manifest it. While it is manifested, acidic slime coats you. A creature that hits you with a melee attack takes Acid damage equal to 1d6 plus your Transformation Stage. Nonmagical ammunition that hits and damages you is destroyed. A nonmagical weapon that damages you or touches you takes a cumulative -1 penalty to attack rolls, and it is destroyed if the penalty reaches -5. Casting Mending on the weapon removes the penalty. By touch, you can also eat through 2 feet of nonmagical wood or metal in 1 minute.",
   "Engulf": "Your Ooze Form lasts 10 minutes when you manifest it. While it is manifested, you can use a Magic action to try to engulf a creature of your size or smaller within 5 feet. The target makes a Strength saving throw against DC 10 plus your Strength modifier plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure, it is engulfed. An engulfed creature has Cover against attacks and effects from outside you, moves along with you, is Restrained, is suffocating, and takes 4d6 Acid damage at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on a success. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points while engulfed is fully digested, leaving no body and no nonmagical gear.",
   "Legion of Slime": "Your Ooze Form lasts until you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest when you manifest it. While it is manifested and an attack hits you and leaves you Bloodied, you can use your Reaction to split into two identical Oozes. Each uses your statistics but is one size smaller, and your current and maximum Hit Points are split evenly between them (round down). Your gear stays on just one of them. Both act on your Initiative and move separately, but together they get only one action, one Bonus Action, and one Reaction per round. Once you use this, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.",
   "Mimic Object": "Your Ooze Form lasts until you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest when you manifest it. While it is manifested, you can use a Magic action to turn into an object of your size or up to two sizes smaller. Worn and carried gear drops into your space. You keep your statistics and look exactly like the object. When a creature touches you in this form, you can use your Reaction to stick to it, leaving it Grappled. The escape DC is 8 plus your Constitution modifier plus your Transformation Stage, and checks to escape have Disadvantage.",
   "Sluggish": "Your body keeps melting and shifting out of your control. Your Speed drops by 5 feet for each Transformation Stage you have reached. You also leave a trail of slime, so ability checks to follow your tracks have Advantage.",
   "Melted Appearance": "Your body is a dripping lump of flesh and slime. You have Disadvantage on Charisma-based ability checks made with the Influence action against creatures that are not Aberrations or Oozes. Your eyes and ears have melted away, so you are permanently Blinded beyond the range of your Blindsight.",
   "Physical Deterioration": "Your skin sloughs off and your bones soften like wax. Sunlight burns and holy light is deadly. You are vulnerable to Radiant damage, and you have Disadvantage on Dexterity ability checks and saving throws.",
   "Slippery Ego": "Your mind is just another part of the slime and loses its grip easily. The first time you become Bloodied after a Long Rest, and whenever you roll a 1 on a saving throw, you lose yourself. You can't cast spells, activate magic items, understand language, or communicate in any intelligible way. Hunger takes over. On your next turn you take the Attack action with melee attacks against a random creature within reach. If none is in reach, you move toward the nearest creature and Dash if needed. At the end of each of your turns you can make a DC 18 Wisdom saving throw to regain your senses. The effect also ends when you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
  },
 },
 "Primordial": {
  "intro": "A spark of primordial chaos has taken root in you, and the elements push against your mortal body. Each stage is a story event, such as absorbing a greater Elemental, touching an elemental node, allying with a being from an Elemental Plane, or freeing an enslaved Elemental. If you die, only a spell of Wish power can bring you back, with or without your Transformation.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain both Stage 1 Boons and the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Primordial Form", "Elemental Affinity"], "d": "Become a Primordial. Gain Primordial Form and Elemental Affinity, plus the Planar Binding Flaw."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon. You also gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 2 Primordial Boon and gain the Roiling Elements Flaw."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon. You also gain the Stage 3 Flaw. Master of Many requires that you already have Dual Nature.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 3 Primordial Boon and gain the Elemental Imbalance Flaw."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon. You also gain the Stage 4 Flaw. Primordial Aura requires Aura of Awakening, and Elemental Mastery requires Master of Many.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 4 Primordial Boon and gain the Primordial Chaos Flaw."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Primordial Form": "You are an Elemental in addition to your other creature types. Your Constitution score increases by 1, to a maximum of 20 from this Boon.",
   "Elemental Affinity": "A single element sparked your change, and it shapes your powers. Choose one element and gain all its benefits. **Air.** You have Resistance to Lightning damage. Once on each of your turns, when you attack with a ranged weapon or ranged spell, you can give that attack Advantage. This does nothing where there is no air, such as underwater or in a vacuum. **Earth.** You have Resistance to Bludgeoning damage. Whenever you gain Temporary Hit Points, you gain extra Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus. **Fire.** You have Resistance to Fire damage. When you deal Fire damage, you can add your Constitution modifier to it. **Water.** You have Resistance to Cold damage. When a creature within 30 feet regains Hit Points, you can use your Reaction to add 1d6 Hit Points to that healing.",
   "Dual Nature": "Add a second element to your Elemental Affinity and gain its benefits.",
   "Elemental Surge": "As a Magic action, you can unleash one of these options. **Lightning Strike.** Make a ranged attack against a creature within 60 feet, using your Constitution modifier and your proficiency. On a hit it takes 3d8 plus your Constitution modifier Lightning damage. You can then use a Bonus Action to repeat the attack on another creature within 30 feet of the first. Damage rises by 1d8 for each Transformation Stage above 2. **Earth Shard.** A creature within 30 feet makes a Constitution saving throw. It takes 3d6 plus your Constitution modifier Bludgeoning damage on a failure, or half on a success. Damage rises by 1d6 for each Stage above 2. You gain Temporary Hit Points equal to half the damage dealt. **Flame Wave.** Each creature in a 15-foot Cone from you makes a Dexterity saving throw against DC 8 plus your Constitution modifier plus your Transformation Stage. It takes 2d8 plus your Constitution modifier Fire damage on a failure. Damage rises by 1d8 for each Stage above 2. **Aquatic Rejuvenation.** A creature you can see within 60 feet regains 2d8 plus your Constitution modifier Hit Points. Healing rises by 1d8 for each Stage above 2. You can use Elemental Surge a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Aura of Awakening": "Your aura awakens the elements in your allies. Choose one option when you gain this Boon, and you can change it after a Long Rest. **Light as Air.** When you or an ally you can see within 30 feet makes a Dexterity saving throw, that creature gains a bonus equal to your Constitution modifier. **Forged in Fire.** When an ally within 10 feet hits with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to make the attack deal Fire damage instead of its normal type, plus 2d6 Fire damage. **Heart of Stone.** You can choose to have Disadvantage on an Initiative check. If you do, you use your Reaction so that you and each creature of your choice within 30 feet gain Temporary Hit Points equal to 1d10 plus your Constitution modifier. While they have those Temporary Hit Points, they can't be Prone unless it comes from Unconscious. **Fluid Movement.** When an ally within 30 feet moves or tries to escape a grapple, you can use your Reaction so that their Speed rises by 10 feet until the end of their turn, their movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks, and they have Advantage on checks to escape the grapple.",
   "Primeval Body": "You no longer need to sleep, breathe, or eat, and you no longer age or suffer the effects of aging. Choose Bludgeoning, Cold, Fire, or Lightning damage. You gain Resistance to it, or Immunity if you already had Resistance.",
   "Master of Many": "Requires Dual Nature. Add a third element to your Elemental Affinity and gain its benefits.",
   "Primordial Aura": "Requires Aura of Awakening. Creatures of your choice within 15 feet gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Cold, Fire, or Lightning damage. Choose the type after a Short Rest or Long Rest, and change it with a Bonus Action. A creature that already has Resistance to that type gains Immunity instead.",
   "Elemental Mastery": "Requires Master of Many. Add the final element to your Elemental Affinity and gain its benefits. You can also wreathe yourself in all four elements. When a creature hits you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to force it to make a Dexterity saving throw. It takes 6d6 damage of a type you choose from Bludgeoning, Cold, Fire, or Lightning, or half as much on a success. After you use this Reaction, your Affinity features improve until the end of your next turn. **Air.** You have Advantage on all ranged weapon and ranged spell attacks. **Earth.** At the start of your turn you gain 20 Temporary Hit Points. **Fire.** At the start of your turn, each creature of your choice within 5 feet takes 2d6 Fire damage. **Water.** When a creature you can see within 60 feet regains Hit Points from spending Hit Point Dice or from a spell or magical ability, it regains 20 extra Hit Points. You can use this a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Planar Binding (Primordial)": "Your body and soul are tied to an Elemental Plane, which tries to pull you in. You have Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws.",
   "Roiling Elements": "The elements inside you strain against your body. You can hold them back and keep a humanoid look, but it takes effort, and stress tends to break the hold. Triggers include becoming Bloodied, being Unconscious, meeting Elemental creatures or powers, being Charmed or Frightened, and using your Primordial Transformation powers. In those moments, or other times of great stress, the GM can call for a Constitution saving throw. The DC is 13 at Stage 2, 16 at Stage 3, and 20 at Stage 4. On a failure your Primordial nature shows, and you have Disadvantage on every D20 Test for 1 minute while you fight for control.",
   "Elemental Imbalance": "Your body reacts badly to harsh elemental damage. When you take Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage, roll 1d6. On a 1, you become volatile. You gain Vulnerability to that instance of damage, even if you had Resistance or Immunity, and creatures within 5 feet of you take the same amount of damage as you took. They can halve it with a DC 15 Constitution saving throw.",
   "Primordial Chaos": "The plane that fuels you pulls harder. Whenever you roll a natural 1 on a saving throw against a spell, you take 8d6 Force damage. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity and comes on top of any normal damage from the effect.",
  },
 },
 "Seraph": {
  "intro": "You are chosen by a higher power to embody a virtue, and you become a Celestial. Each stage is a story event, such as defeating a great force of darkness, creating a hallowed landmark, founding a parish, or redeeming a soul thought lost. You can drop all Boons and Flaws at any time by relinquishing your divinity, but regaining the power may be hard.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain Celestial Form and one other Stage 1 Boon of your choice. You also gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Celestial Form"], "d": "Become a Seraph. Gain Celestial Form, one more Stage 1 Boon, and the Planar Binding Flaw."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon. You also gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 2 Seraph Boon and gain the Blinding Radiance Flaw."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon. You also gain the Stage 3 Flaw. Cleanse Affliction requires Divine Clemency, and Protective Wings requires Angelic Wings.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 3 Seraph Boon and gain the Beacon to Darkness Flaw."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon. You also gain the Stage 4 Flaw. Bow of Celestial Domination requires Bow of Celestial Judgement.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Choose a Stage 4 Seraph Boon and gain the Seraph Corruption Flaw."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Celestial Form": "You are a Celestial in addition to your other creature types, and you have Resistance to Radiant damage.",
   "Angelic Wings": "As a Bonus Action, you can manifest feathered wings for 1 hour. While they are out and you are not wearing heavy armor, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. You can manifest them a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage and regain all uses after a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
   "Holy Strikes": "When you hit with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, or damage a creature with a cantrip, you can add 1d6 Radiant damage. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage, and you regain all uses after a Short Rest or Long Rest. The extra damage grows with your Stage: 2d6 at Stage 2, 3d6 at Stage 3, and 4d6 at Stage 4.",
   "Divine Clemency": "When an ally you can see within 30 feet takes damage, you can use your Reaction to cast Healing Word on them at 1st level without a spell slot. You can do this a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Sacred Retribution": "When an ally you can see within 30 feet takes the Attack action with a weapon or Unarmed Strike, you can use your Reaction to fill them with zeal and let them make one extra attack. On a hit, the target takes an extra 1d8 Radiant damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Cleanse Affliction": "Requires Divine Clemency. When you use Divine Clemency on a creature, it also gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage healed by Healing Word, gains Advantage on its next D20 Test within 1 minute, and you end one of these conditions on it: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, or Poisoned.",
   "Protective Wings": "Requires Angelic Wings. While your wings are manifested, you can use your Reaction when you or an ally within 5 feet is targeted by a weapon attack to impose Disadvantage on it. If the attack hits the ally, you take half the damage (round up) and the ally takes the rest. You also have Advantage on saving throws and ability checks to avoid or escape a grapple, and your Fly Speed rises by 10 feet.",
   "Bow of Celestial Judgement": "As a Bonus Action, you can manifest a bow of divine light for 1 minute. While it is out, you can use a Magic action to target a creature you can see within 120 feet. It makes a Dexterity saving throw against DC 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. It takes 6d6 Radiant damage on a failure, or 10d6 if it is a Fey, Fiend, or Undead, and half as much on a success. You also have Resistance to Necrotic damage and gain 5 Temporary Hit Points at the start of each of your turns. You can manifest the bow a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Aura of Holy Purge": "You emit a 20-foot Emanation of righteous fervor, unless you are Unconscious. When an ally in the aura hits with a weapon attack, they can use their Reaction to make it a Critical Hit. If they do, you and that ally each gain a level of Exhaustion. That ally can't use this again until they finish a Long Rest.",
   "Aura of Righteous Mercy": "You emit a 20-foot Emanation of peace, unless you are Unconscious. When an ally in the aura would drop to 0 Hit Points, they can use their Reaction to drop to 1 Hit Point instead. If they do, you and that ally each gain a level of Exhaustion. That ally can't use this again until they finish a Long Rest.",
   "Bow of Celestial Domination": "Requires Bow of Celestial Judgement. While your bow is manifested, your Magic action can also affect a second creature within 10 feet of the first target. You are immune to Necrotic damage instead of resistant, and you gain 15 Temporary Hit Points at the start of each of your turns instead of 5.",
   "Planar Binding (Seraph)": "Your body and soul are bound to the higher planes of good, which try to draw your soul to its final reward. You have Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws.",
   "Blinding Radiance": "Your body glows with divine light. Your eyes may become hollow braziers, or extra wings may unsettle mortals. You can suppress this and look like your old humanoid self, but it takes effort, and stress or wrath tends to break it. Triggers include becoming Bloodied, being Unconscious, witnessing evil, meeting Fiendish creatures or powers, and using your Seraph powers for the first time after a Short Rest or Long Rest. In those moments, or other times of great stress, the GM can call for a Constitution saving throw. The DC is 13 at Stage 2, 16 at Stage 3, and 20 at Stage 4. On a failure your radiance shows. Each non-enemy creature within 30 feet that can see you must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma saving throw or be Blinded for 1 minute, and attacks against you have Advantage for 1 minute.",
   "Beacon to Darkness": "Evil is drawn to your virtue. When you or an ally within 30 feet commits an evil act, such as murdering innocents, you become Corrupted. The GM decides what counts as evil. While Corrupted, you have Disadvantage on attack rolls against evil creatures and on saving throws against spells or effects from evil creatures. An ally who caused your Corruption is not your ally, and you are not theirs, until it is removed. You remove Corrupted by finishing a Short Rest or Long Rest in which you pray for at least 1 hour and burn holy incense or give at least 100 GP times your Transformation Stage to a good local cause.",
   "Seraph Corruption": "The evil of the world weighs on you and sometimes breaks you. Whenever you roll a natural 1 on a saving throw, you suffer these effects for 1 minute. At the start of each of your turns you take 1d10 Psychic damage that nothing can reduce. You can't regain Hit Points or have Temporary Hit Points. You have Disadvantage on the first attack you make each round. Once per round, the first creature you force to make a saving throw against your spell has Advantage on it.",
  },
 },
}
